    "result_text": "All 267 tests pass with BUILD SUCCESS. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the registration-date default for owner creation. When an owner is created without a registration date, it's set to today's date and returned in the owner response as `registrationDate` in ISO format (YYYY-MM-DD).\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`Owner` entity** (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 added a `LocalDate registrationDate` field mapped to a new `registration_date` column, with getter/setter.\n\n2. **Database schemas** \u2014 added the nullable `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table in all four dialects (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`). Tests run on the `hsqldb` profile.\n\n3. **OpenAPI spec** (`openapi.yml`) \u2014 added a `registrationDate` property (`type: string, format: date, readOnly: true`) to the `Owner` response schema, which generates a `LocalDate` field on `OwnerDto` that Jackson serializes as `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\n4. **`BuildOwner` function** \u2014 after mapping the request, defaults `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` when null. Since `registrationDate` isn't part of the editable `OwnerFields` input, this always applies on creation.\n\n5. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 the response mapping (`toOwnerDto`) picks up `registrationDate` automatically by name; added an explicit `ignore` for it on the `OwnerFieldsDto \u2192 Owner` mapping, consistent with the existing `id`/`pets` ignores.\n\nThe Cp08 acceptance test (`registrationDate` defaults to today) passes, and the full suite (267 tests) remains green.",
